<figure class="scaling-research l-body-outset" aria-label="Methodological research shapes the scaling rate and the axes">
    <div class="scaling-research-panels">
      <div class="scaling-research-panel">
        <h3>Improve the scaling rate</h3>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 440 245" role="img" aria-labelledby="scaling-law-title scaling-law-desc">
          <title id="scaling-law-title">Methods change the return on scale</title>
          <desc id="scaling-law-desc">A schematic log-log plot compares existing methods with better methods. The steeper line represents a larger scaling exponent, so performance improves faster as resources increase.</desc>
          <path class="scaling-axis" d="M55 37 V195 H418" />
          <text x="55" y="23">Performance (log)</text>
          <text x="418" y="224" text-anchor="end">Resources (log)</text>
          <path class="scaling-baseline" d="M72 180 L396 120" />
          <path class="scaling-improved" d="M72 180 L396 57" />
          <text class="scaling-accent" x="235" y="62">Better methods</text>
          <text class="scaling-muted" x="262" y="160">Existing methods</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
      <div class="scaling-research-panel">
        <h3>Define the axes</h3>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 440 245" role="img" aria-labelledby="scaling-axes-title scaling-axes-desc">
          <title id="scaling-axes-title">Research defines what to scale and what to improve</title>
          <desc id="scaling-axes-desc">The vertical axis asks what should improve, for example reliability. The horizontal axis asks what to scale, for example experience from interacting with the world.</desc>
          <path class="scaling-axis" d="M55 37 V195 H418" />
          <text class="scaling-accent" x="55" y="23">What should improve?</text>
          <text class="scaling-muted" x="72" y="61">e.g., reliability</text>
          <path class="scaling-direction" d="M90 166 L280 78 M269 78 H280 V89" />
          <text class="scaling-muted" x="418" y="179" text-anchor="end">e.g., experience</text>
          <text class="scaling-accent" x="418" y="224" text-anchor="end">What can we scale?</text>
        </svg>
      </div>
    </div>
</figure>
